<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n114335" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χολέρ-α</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χολέρ-ρη</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cholera,</i> a
			disease in which the humours of the body (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χολή,
				χολαί</span>) are violently discharged by vomiting and stool,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Coac.</u>
				117
			</span></i>, <u>Acut.</u>(<u>Sp.</u>) <i><span class="en">
				49
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SA</u>
				2.5
			</span></i>; but, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξηρὴ χολέρη</span> obstinate
				<i>obstruction,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Acut.</u>
			</span></i>(<i>Sp.).</i><i><span class="en">
				48
			</span></i>. (Fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χολή</span> acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Cels.
				4.18(11)
			</span></i>, but fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χολάς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Alex.Trall.
				8.1
			</span></i>.) </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>nausea,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔσται ὑμῖν εἰς χολέραν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Nu.</u>
					11.20
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χολέδρα</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
